WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're hanging out with

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.567
the one and only
Michael Strahan!

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:09.033
Now, we always like to do
something a little competitive

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.934
when you're on the show,
so I thought it would be fun

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.300
to go head-to-head with
some 30-second challenges.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.033
It is time for "30 Seconds To."

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:18.467
-♪ 30 seconds to ♪

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.367
-This first challenge --
we have 30 seconds to try

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.801
and stack these cranberry sauces
into a pyramid.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:28.267
Whoever finishes their pyramid
first wins the challenge.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.400
Are you a cranberry sauce dude
on Thanksgiving?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.767
-Yes, I am.
-Can or fresh?

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:34.868
-Can is always consistent.
I'm not gonna lie.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.868
And I like cutting
along the lines.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.100
Oh, I'm not the only one.
I know it.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.801
[ Laughter ]
-I like it too, yeah.

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.534
I like it when my sauce has abs.
Okay.

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.534
We're gonna get 30 seconds
on the clock.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:49.801
We're gonna have to make
a pyramid out of these.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.868
-A pyramid? So you have to
use every one, right?

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.667
-Yes, you have to use
every one of these.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.133
Alright. You ready?

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:57.801
-Yeah.
-Set, go.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:06.701
♪♪

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:07.968
This is going to be tough.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:11.000
♪♪

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.667
What are you doing, man?
You know what's up, dude.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:17.434
Come on, bud.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.501
What's going on?

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:22.467
-Do they have --
-Come on. Yeah, you can do it.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.267
You can let it go.
-Hold on, hold up, 4.

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.901
Aaah!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.434
-No, you got that.
You got to give it right there.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:30.868
Points. No, respect.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.300
Respect to Michael Strahan
right there.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.567
You can take that away.
-There you go.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.701
-Ooh, that tastes good.
-Can't wait to what's next.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.000
-Alright. Here we go. Alright.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.501
This next challenge, we're going
to have 30 seconds to see

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:46.334
who can get a meat thermometer
the hottest by blowing onto it

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:47.701
as fast as we can.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:54.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.567
Dude, you had a great reputation
up to this point.

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:02.067
So, these are meat thermometers.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.234
So it's a real one.
67 degrees in here.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.701
-Why is mine 64 1/2?
I'm already started --

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.968
-Nah, 'cause you're cool.
-All I got to say is whoever

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.167
came up with this stuff
needs to really get a life.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.601
-It was me. Alright. Here we go.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:18.968
Let's get 30 seconds
on the clock.

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.234
I don't know how to do it.
Ready?

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:22.701
How do we do it?

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.334
Ready? Sorry. Set.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:27.267
-No, you're not starting
a campfire like that.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.501
-Alright, hold on.
Where you at now?

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:32.267
I'm 75 already.
-60 -- 70.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.601
-Alright. Here we go. Ready?

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.667
Ready, set, go.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:38.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:45.334
♪♪

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:51.767
♪♪

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.200
[ Coughing ]

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.367
♪♪

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:58.767
[ Jimmy yelling ]

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:07.167
♪♪

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:09.767
[ Buzzer ]
What do we got?

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.734
83, wow!

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.334
-Yeah!
[ Dinging ]

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:16.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:17.901
-I almost died on that,
by the way.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.934
-I thought we were going to,
like, pass out.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.634
But, you know, everybody always
says, you're full of hot air.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.701
Now I know I am.
-Alright, not bad. Good job.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.300
-There we go.
-Alright, perfect.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.501
Now we're down to
our final challenge.

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.200
Man, I'm light-headed
right here.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.133
Yeah, we have 30 seconds
to see who can toss

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.567
the most ears of corn
into our mouths.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:39.234
It's literal corn hole.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:40.334
[ Applause ]

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.300
Whoever --

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.501
Whoever gets the most corn
in the hole...

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.634
...wins the round
and the whole game.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.734
-It's like always something
with the gap, man.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:58.968
Always.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.834
-You ready for this?
Let's try this.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.133
Get 30 seconds on the clock.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.400
Congratulations. Good luck.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.901
Whoever wins this
wins the whole thing.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.901
-I'm going to tell my mom
to go to bed early tonight.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.734
-On your mark, get set, go.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:20.234
♪♪

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:31.167
♪♪

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:32.601
-Oh, come on!

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.100
♪♪

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:42.000
♪♪

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.133
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:48.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.601
-Michael Strahan!
-Yeah!

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:53.133
[ Dinging ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:56.367
-Come on!
Michael Strahan, the champ.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:05:00.400
His Michael Strahan Daily
Defense skin care is available

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.100
on Amazon and
michaelstrahanskin.com.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.467
Chef Daniel Humm joins us
after the break.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.467
Stick around, everybody.

